## Prerequisites

[Explicit Forward Proxy must be enabled and configured](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/global-secure-access/how-to-custom-proxy-file-hosting#prerequisites), including licensing, TLS inspection and access policies. The example declares `depends_on` on [network_explicit_forward_proxy](graph_beta_identity_and_access_network_explicit_forward_proxy.md). If that singleton is already managed in Terraform, reference the existing resource or module instead of declaring a duplicate. If managed externally, configure it before applying this resource.

The PAC's `is_enabled` controls its availability to clients independently of EFP enablement. Destroy deletes the PAC, but destroying the EFP resource leaves the proxy configuration unchanged.

## PAC File Considerations

Public PAC URLs are service-generated and are not exposed by this resource. Changes to a file can affect clients using it; cached copies can delay their effect.

`${GSAEFP}` remains literal in stored content and is substituted when served. Use `$${GSAEFP}` in an HCL string or heredoc; a file loaded with `file()` needs no escaping. A tenant can host up to 20 files.

Reusing a deleted PAC name can return HTTP 409. Use a fresh unique name when recreating a file; the service's name-retention period is unknown.

